  urldate = {2025-10-23},
  abstract = {Physically Related Function (PRef) was a concept coined by Secured Embedded Architecture Laboratory, IIT Kharagpur, where we took the idea of PUFs and looked at it from a different view point. While in PUFs we utilize the fact that every pair of device has a unique device physics and hence unique responses, in PRefs we focus on the similarities, implying these pairs do produce 'related' responses for some challenges. Based on this we wrote a paper at IEEE TIFS, https://lnkd.in/db6cJuav We also delivered a big Government project using this idea.  Many times the story ends here. But seems here there is more to it! Very happy to see this idea being reproduced and improved by a German research group led by  Karlsruhe Institute of Technology, Karlsruhe, Germany, https://lnkd.in/duwTTfRb It does not happen every day, one starts an original idea from  scratch, and other groups like, reproduce, improve, and write papers in top-tier venues. This paper is published in ACM TECS, a flagship journal. Looking forward to more works on PRefs. Tagging my (ex)students, and colleague who had been co-authors/co-workers in all the present PReF papers: Harishma Boyapally, Durba Chatterjee, Urbi Chatterjee, Sikhar Patranabis, Aritra Hazra, Siddhartha Chowdhury, Shreya Gangopadhyay, Anupam Mondal, Chandan Kumar},
